      "id": 18,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Parties per host and per key (status only)",
      "description": "Per-key and per-host counts carry no metric labels on purpose (a job array can invent thousands of keys). Use `nsm status` or GET /v1/status for them.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 18,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Per-key and per-host breakdowns are deliberately **not** metrics: a rendezvous key or a host as a label would create one time series per value, and a job array can invent thousands. Ask the broker instead:\n\n```\nnsm status ADMIN            # keys and hosts tables\nnsm status ADMIN --parties  # one row per party\ncurl -s http://ADMIN/v1/status | jq .keys\n```\n\nSee `docs/MONITORING.md`."
      }
